# Cloudflare Pages headers stub - INERT on GitHub Pages (the current host).
#
# NOT THE LIVE POLICY. GitHub Pages ignores this file and does not copy it into
# docs/, so none of the headers below are enforced on the live site. The single
# live, canonical security policy is the <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-
# Policy"> tag in web/templates/base.html. Edit that tag to change the live CSP;
# this file is aspirational only.
#
# The live GitHub Pages response carries just Strict-Transport-Security
# (1 year). The HTTP-only headers below (X-Content-Type-Options, frame-ancestors
# via X-Frame-Options, Permissions-Policy, COOP/CORP) cannot be expressed as
# <meta> tags and are therefore simply absent live. See
# audit/11_spa_structural_audit.md spa-S2 / S4 / S5.
#
# This file is kept so that IF the apex is ever moved to Cloudflare Pages (or
# fronted by a Cloudflare Worker) the full header set lands without a second
# source change. While on GitHub Pages, do NOT remove the base.html meta CSP:
# it is the only thing enforcing a policy at all.
#
# References:
#   audit/11_spa_structural_audit.md
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# To activate (only after migrating the apex off GitHub Pages):
#   1. Configure Cloudflare Pages with publish directory = docs/
#   2. Either move this file to docs/_headers, or update web/build.py to
#      copy it there as part of the build (alongside the _copy_static
#      shutil.copytree call).
#   3. Only THEN reconcile with base.html: once these HTTP headers are live,
#      the meta CSP can defer to the policy below as the single source.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org https://server.arcgisonline.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://giscus.app; connect-src 'self' https://giscus.app; frame-src https://giscus.app; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Photos and static assets are public records intentionally served with
# permissive CORS so syndication tools can fetch them. Inmate photos are
# public under ORC 149.43; data files (search.json, dispatches.json, RSS)
# are licensed CC BY-NC 4.0 per audit/00_index.md and the data page footer.
/photos/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin

/static/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/feed.xml
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/booked.xml
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/released.xml
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Search and dispatch JSON used by the homepage; same caching as RSS.
/search.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/dispatches.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
